    {
        "id": "speed-demo-intro-text",
        "type": "ui-template",
        "z": "speed-two-methods-demo",
        "group": "speed-demo-intro",
        "page": "",
        "ui": "",
        "name": "Intro: Four ways to use CalcsLive",
        "order": 1,
        "width": 12,
        "height": 0,
        "head": "",
        "format": "<template>\n<div class=\"pa-2\" style=\"line-height:1.6\">\n<p class=\"mb-3\">Explore four ways to run CalcsLive calculations from Node-RED. A–C use the same speed calculator; D lets you choose an article from the dashboard.</p>\n<ul style=\"padding-left:22px\">\n<li><strong>A — Form inputs:</strong> Enter distance, time and units in a dashboard form. Node-RED prepares the data and sends it to CalcsLive.</li>\n<li><strong>B — JSON inside CalcsLive:</strong> Configure input values and output units in the CalcsLive node, then trigger it with the dashboard button or an Inject node.</li>\n<li><strong>C — Dashboard JSON editor:</strong> Edit the Inputs and Outputs JSON on the dashboard and run the speed calculation.</li>\n<li><strong>D — Choose your article:</strong> Enter a CalcsLive Article ID and its Inputs and Outputs JSON on the dashboard. View the first requested output on a gauge and open the linked article.</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"mt-3 mb-0\">CalcsLive accepts upstream values in their original units, handles the calculation and unit conversion, and returns\nresults in the units you request for display or downstream nodes.</p>\n\n<p class=\"mt-3 mb-0\">In other words, you can offload unit conversion and calculation from you flow to CalcsLive and enjoyr full Unit Freedom.</p>\n</div>\n</template>",
